course: dictionary
lesson: 4417
title: Halving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To halve something is to cut it, or share it, into two equal parts. Halving means the same as dividing by 2. «Halve the cake» means cut it into two equal pieces.
explain: To halve an amount is to make it half as big. «The price was halved» means it became half of what it was before. Halved is the past form, as in «I halved the apple».
explain: Halving undoes doubling, and doubling undoes halving. «Undo doubled by halving» means that if a number was doubled, you halve it to get back to where you started. Use this to check your sums.
explain: «If two ages add up to 20 and one child is 4 years older, take the 4 away and halve» gives 8 and 12. Halving can help you solve hard problems step by step.
fact: Halve means to cut into two equal parts, or to divide by 2.
fact: Halves, halved and halving are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Halve» can also mean to make an amount half as big, as in «halved the price».
fact: Halving undoes doubling: 6 doubled is 12, and 12 halved is 6.
fact: «Guessing a number from 1 to 100 by halving never needs more than 7 guesses, because 2 multiplied by itself 7 times is 128.»
exercise: «Halve the cake so each child gets the same amount.» What does halve mean here? | Throw it away | Eat it all at once | *Cut into two equal parts | Make it bigger
exercise: «The price was halved in the sale.» What happened to the price? | It stayed the same | It went up | It doubled | *It became half as big
exercise: «Learning a family together halves the work.» Find and copy the word that means the work is cut in two. | work | *halves | learning | family
test: What is 8 halved? | 80 | 16 | *4 | 2
test: Aisha says «halve» means «double». Is she right? | *No, halve means make half as big, the opposite of doubling | Yes, halve and double mean the same | Only when you are sharing sweets | No, halve means add two
exam: To undo «doubled», what should you do? | Take away 5 | Add 2 | Double it again | *Halve it
